From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0415-mem-02-lazy-present.patch

Source: 0415-mem-02-lazy-present.patch
Core patch: paths relative to core16, through 0181. Also compatible with the
frontend patch list through 0410: none changes these two files.
Off by default. Enable with EDEN_PS5_LAZY_PRESENT=1 in env.txt. Only the exact
value 1 enables it; unset, 0, and other values keep eager allocation.

Proven source ownership: Layer::ConfigureDraw selects the cached GPU image for
accelerated display, but RefreshResources allocates a staging buffer and N raw
images anyway. These are VMA application allocations outside the image and
buffer caches reported by EDEN_REFUSED_IMAGES / EDEN_REFUSED_BUFFERS.

Saving, conditional on accelerated presentation: N * stride * height * bpp
staging bytes plus N raw-image allocations (including driver padding). At
3840x2160 RGBA8, stride 3840 and N=3, that is 189.84 MiB before image padding.
Run101 stderr.log:9745 has a 94 MiB host-visible allocation, consistent with
that staging buffer, not proof of its identity. The 3840x2160 cached images are
logged at :828-830. Neither the swapchain image count nor accelerated-hit rate
is measured by those lines. Do not advertise 190 MiB as measured savings.

Keep resource ticks even without raw storage: descriptors and AA still use
per-image slots. Switching to CPU upload allocates full-size storage before
use. Switching back waits every recorded tick before releasing it; queued
upload lambdas capture this Layer. Size, stride and format changes also wait.
Release image views before their images. No texture levels or pixels change.
A stream of alternating CPU/GPU frames can cause waits and allocation churn.

Validation: git apply --check against core16 passed. Changed routines passed
Apple clang 21 -std=c++20 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -fsyntax-only with stub types;
constexpr checks covered repeated GPU frames, CPU fallback, return to GPU,
stride/size/format changes and tick waits. This is not a full-file/PS5 compile.
No console or full PS5 build was run.
This removes redundant backing, but does not establish a cure for exhaustion.

Assisted-by: Codex (local audit and draft; not submitted upstream)

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/present/layer.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/present/layer.cpp
index 5652090bd7..1469565ff9 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/present/layer.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/present/layer.cpp
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
 // SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright 2024 yuzu Emulator Project
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
 
+#include <cstdlib>
+#include <cstring>
 #include <variant>
 #include "video_core/present.h"
 #include "video_core/renderer_vulkan/present/anti_alias_pass.h"
@@ -103,7 +105,14 @@ void Layer::ConfigureDraw(const Device& device, PresentPushConstants* out_push_c
         (framebuffer.layer_stack_mask & Service::Nvnflinger::LayerStackBit(
                                             Service::Nvnflinger::LayerStackId::Recording)) == 0;
 
-    RefreshResources(device, framebuffer);
+    // The cached GPU image is already the source of accelerated presentation. Raw
+    // upload images and their staging buffer are needed only by the CPU fallback.
+    // Keep this opt-in until accelerated/fallback transitions have run on PS5.
+    static const bool lazy_raw = [] {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_PS5_LAZY_PRESENT");
+        return value != nullptr && std::strcmp(value, "1") == 0;
+    }();
+    RefreshResources(device, framebuffer, !lazy_raw || !use_accelerated);
     SetAntiAliasPass(device);
 #ifdef HAS_RESHADE
     SetPostProcessPass(device, is_applet);
@@ -191,7 +200,6 @@ void Layer::CreateStagingBuffer(const Device& device, const Tegra::FramebufferCo
 
 void Layer::CreateRawImages(const Device& device, const Tegra::FramebufferConfig& framebuffer) {
     const auto format = GetFormat(framebuffer);
-    resource_ticks.resize(image_count);
     raw_images.resize(image_count);
     raw_image_views.resize(image_count);
 
@@ -202,20 +210,32 @@ void Layer::CreateRawImages(const Device& device, const Tegra::FramebufferConfig
     }
 }
 
-void Layer::RefreshResources(const Device& device, const Tegra::FramebufferConfig& framebuffer) {
-    if (framebuffer.width == raw_width && framebuffer.height == raw_height &&
-        framebuffer.pixel_format == pixel_format && !raw_images.empty()) {
+void Layer::RefreshResources(const Device& device, const Tegra::FramebufferConfig& framebuffer,
+                             bool need_raw_images) {
+    const bool same_shape = framebuffer.width == raw_width && framebuffer.height == raw_height &&
+                            framebuffer.stride == raw_stride &&
+                            framebuffer.pixel_format == pixel_format;
+    if (same_shape && resource_ticks.size() == image_count &&
+        need_raw_images == !raw_images.empty()) {
         return;
     }
 
+    // Wait for every descriptor/AA user too, even when no raw image was made.
+    // A queued CPU upload captures this Layer, so it must finish before reset.
+    ReleaseRawImages();
+    resource_ticks.assign(image_count, 0);
     raw_width = framebuffer.width;
     raw_height = framebuffer.height;
+    raw_stride = framebuffer.stride;
     pixel_format = framebuffer.pixel_format;
-    anti_alias.emplace<std::monostate>();
-
-    ReleaseRawImages();
-    CreateStagingBuffer(device, framebuffer);
-    CreateRawImages(device, framebuffer);
+    if (!same_shape) {
+        anti_alias.emplace<std::monostate>();
+    }
+    if (need_raw_images) {
+        // Allocate before UpdateRawImage can run. Size and format are unchanged.
+        CreateStagingBuffer(device, framebuffer);
+        CreateRawImages(device, framebuffer);
+    }
 }
 
 void Layer::SetAntiAliasPass(const Device& device) {
@@ -287,6 +307,7 @@ void Layer::ReleaseRawImages() {
     for (const u64 tick : resource_ticks) {
         scheduler.Wait(tick);
     }
+    raw_image_views.clear();
     raw_images.clear();
     buffer.reset();
 }
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/present/layer.h b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/present/layer.h
